menu "Bluetooth Audio (Bridge Mode)"

config BT_A2DP_ENABLE
    bool "Enable Bluetooth A2DP bridge mode (ESP32-S3)"
    default n
    help
        Enable Bluetooth A2DP audio bridge functionality for ESP32-S3.
        Since ESP32-S3 does not have Classic BT hardware, this enables
        bridge mode: the main controller proxies BT requests via UART
        to an ESP32 Bridge device which has Classic BT / A2DP support.

        This registers /bt/status, /bt/scan, /bt/connect, /bt/disconnect,
        /bt/forget, and /bt/bridge_status HTTP API endpoints on the
        configuration portal, allowing users to scan and connect
        Bluetooth speakers through the ESP32 Bridge.

endmenu
